---
title: Password Reset
---
%% Forgot-password → emailed link → new password. The security property worth noticing is
%% step 5: the response is identical whether or not the account exists.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>ResetPasswordComponent
    participant API as UserController<br/>/user
    participant SVC as UserService
    participant DB as MySQL
    participant MAIL as EmailService

    rect rgba(107, 91, 255, 0.10)
    note over U, MAIL: Phase 1 — request the link
    U->>SPA: Enter account email
    SPA->>API: GET /user/resetpassword/{email}
    API->>SVC: resetPassword(email)

    alt account exists
        SVC->>DB: INSERT resetpasswordverifications<br/>(url key + expiry)
        SVC->>MAIL: Send reset link (UI_APP_URL/verify/password/{key})
    else no such account
        SVC-->>SVC: Do nothing — silently
    end

    API-->>SPA: 200 OK — identical body either way
    note right of API: No user enumeration.<br/>A different response for<br/>"unknown email" would turn<br/>this into an account oracle.
    end

    rect rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.10)
    note over U, MAIL: Phase 2 — follow the link
    U->>U: Open email, click reset link
    U->>SPA: Navigate /verify/password/{key}
    SPA->>API: GET /user/verify/password/{key}
    API->>SVC: verifyPasswordKey(key)
    SVC->>DB: SELECT ... WHERE url = :key
    alt key valid and unexpired
        API-->>SPA: 200 OK — render the new-password form
    else expired or unknown
        API-->>SPA: 400 — link is no longer valid
    end
    end

    rect rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.10)
    note over U, MAIL: Phase 3 — set the new password
    U->>SPA: Enter new password + confirmation
    SPA->>API: PUT /user/new/password<br/>{key, password, confirmPassword}
    API->>SVC: renewPassword(form)
    SVC->>SVC: Validate against PasswordPolicy
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE users SET password (BCrypt, strength 12)
    SVC->>DB: DELETE the verification row — single use
    API-->>SPA: 200 OK
    SPA->>U: Redirect to /login
    end
